// Demonstrates: a command with no name at all — "<<" immediately followed by its own closing
// ">>", so the token where a name was expected is the command's end token, not text. Distinct
// from unknown-command.dlb, where a name IS present but unrecognized. Followed by an unrelated
// second error, to prove resync here doesn't over- or under-consume.
title: Start
speaker: Narrator
---
<<>>
<<sett $x = 1>>
===
